pain:
  narrative: You manage 2,500+ vehicles—trucks, vans, specialized equipment—spread across multiple depots and regions. Fuel is your largest variable cost. You don't have visibility into consumption patterns by driver, route, or vehicle type. Maintenance is reactive—you don't know a transmission is failing until the truck breaks down on a delivery, missing your SLA and costing you a penalty. Your analytics are fragmented—GPS data lives in one system, fuel data in another, maintenance in a third. You can't correlate a driver's speeding habit with fuel waste, or match vehicle age against failure rates.
